  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "The frozen existential assertion in source.md is true.  Let h have ordered real basis (e1,e2,r,z), with the only nonzero brackets up to skew-symmetry [e1,e2]=e1+z, [e1,r]=-r, and [z,r]=r.  Let V=span(e1,e2,r) and q=Rz.  This bracket satisfies Jacobi, V Lie-generates h, and kappa_q vanishes on V.  Every complement of V is q_(x,y,t)=R(z-xe1-ye2-tr); its vertical trace character on (e1,e2,r) is (-y,x,0), while its horizontal trace character on the displayed generator is 1+x+y.  Thus vertical balance forces x=y=0, where horizontal balance fails, so no complement of V is modularly balanced.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
